<title>BULGARIA: Yield falls to 1.71 pct on Bulgaria 4-wk T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls to 1.71 pct on Bulgaria 4-wk T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yield fell further on Bulgaria's Finance Ministry issue of 18 billion levs of four-week discount T-bills at the daily auction on Thursday as the issue was heavily oversubscribed, central bank figures showed on Friday.</p>
<p>The average yield to maturity on the issue was 1.71 percent, down from 2.57 percent on Wednesday and 2.93 percent on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with no minimum acceptable price set in advance.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		  BG3038497007</p>
<p> Maturity			four weeks</p>
<p> Par value		     18,000 million levs</p>
<p> Issue date		    June 13</p>
<p> Maturity date		 July 11</p>
<p> Bids received		 65,308.6 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	   97.97 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		 18,000 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	  98.32 pct</p>
<p> Avg yield to maturity     1.71 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 91188</p>
</text>
